            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.mathgenealogy.org/id.php?id=212986"} MathGenealogy page
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            Suggestion to understand the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Veneziano+amplitude"} Veneziano amplitude
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitude"} scattering amplitude
            of chains of particles with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/harmonic+oscillator"} harmonic
            nearest-neighbour interaction, in the continuum limit described by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"} Polyakov action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            (alongside
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+gauge-string+duality"} Polyakov gauge-string duality
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"}> Leonard Susskind
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Structure of Hadrons Implied by Duality
              %strong 1
              (1970) 1182 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.1.1182"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.1.1182
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Early suggestion that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            is described by regarding the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
            as
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "AdS-QCD+correspondence#PolyakovGaugeStringDualityReferences"} gauge/string duality
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Kogut"}> John Kogut
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Vacuum polarization and the absence of free quarks in four dimensions
                %strong 9
                (1974) 3501-3512 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.9.3501"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.9.3501
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Kogut"}> John Kogut
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hamiltonian formulation of Wilson’s lattice gauge theories
                %strong 11
                (1975) 395 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.11.395"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.11.395
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p “The gauge-invariant configuration space consists of a collection of strings with quarks at their ends. The strings are lines of non-Abelian electric flux. In the strong coupling limit the dynamics is best described in terms of these strings. Quark confinement is a result of the inability to break a string without producing a pair. &amp;lbrack;…&amp;rbrack;”
                %p “The confining mechanism is the appearance of one dimensional electric flux tubes which must link separated quarks. The appropriate description of the strongly coupled limit consists of a theory of interacting, propagating strings. &amp;lbrack;…&amp;rbrack;”
                %p “This picture of the strongly coupled Yang-Mills theory in terms of a collection of stringlike flux lines is the central result of our analysis. It should be compared with the phenomenological use of stringlike degrees of freedom which has been widely used in describing hadrons.”
          %p
            Introducing the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
          %ul
            %li#Susskind94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"}> Leonard Susskind
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The World as a hologram
              %strong 36
              (1995) 6377-6396 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9409089"}> hep-th/9409089
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.531249"} doi:10.1063/1.531249
          %p
            Introducing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-brane"} D0-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
          %ul
            %li#BanksFischlerShenkerSusskind96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Banks"}> Tom Banks
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Willy+Fischler"} Willy Fischler
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Shenker"} Stephen Shenker
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
                %em M Theory As A Matrix Model: A Conjecture
                Phys. Rev. D55 (1997). (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9610043"}> arXiv:hep-th/9610043
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"}> Leonard Susskind
                ,
                %em Another Conjecture about M(atrix) Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9704080"}> arXiv:hep-th/9704080
                )
          %p
            In view of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+space+holography"} flat space holography
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"}> Leonard Susskind
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Holography in the flat space limit
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/482388"} spire
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9901079"} arXiv:hep-th/9901079
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1301570"} doi:10.1063/1.1301570
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes+in+string+theory"} black holes in string theory
            via the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Banks"}> Tom Banks
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Willy+Fischler"} Willy Fischler
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Klebanov"} Igor Klebanov
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Schwarzschild Black Holes from Matrix Theory
                %strong 80
                (1998) 226-229 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9709091"}> arXiv:hep-th/9709091
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Banks"}> Tom Banks
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Willy+Fischler"} Willy Fischler
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Klebanov"} Igor Klebanov
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Schwarzchild Black Holes in Matrix Theory II
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711005"} arXiv:hep-th/9711005
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Klebanov"}> Igor Klebanov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Schwarzschild Black Holes in Various Dimensions from Matrix Theory
                %strong 416
                62-66 (1998) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9709108"}> arXiv:hep-th/9709108
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Introducing the notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/giant+gravitons"} giant gravitons
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+McGreevy"}> John McGreevy
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Leonard Susskind
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolaos+Toumbas"} Nicolaos Toumbas
              = succeed "," do
                %em Invasion of the Giant Gravitons from Anti-de Sitter Space
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0003075"} arXiv:hep-th/0003075
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+effect"} fractional quantum Hall effect
            via a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative
